{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 96}
{meta: public_domain Traditional English ballad; this text follows versions collected and published in the 19th century (e.g. Frank Kidson, 1891). Not the 1966 Simon & Garfunkel arrangement.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Are you going to [G]Scarborough [Am]Fair?[Am]
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[C]mary and [D]thyme;[D]
[Am]Remember [C]me to one who [G]lives there,[G]
[Am]For once she [G]was a true love of [Am]mine.[Am]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Tell her to make me a [G]cambric [Am]shirt,[Am]
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[C]mary and [D]thyme;[D]
[Am]Without no [C]seams nor needle[G]work,[G]
[Am]Then she'll [G]be a true love of [Am]mine.[Am]
{end_of_verse}
